  "reasoning": "Cook\u2019s statewide Partisan Voting Index rates Michigan as EV+0, indicating a structurally even state at the presidential level.[1] Recent cycle handicapping from the Almanac of American Politics and Sabato-style analysis has shifted the 2026 Michigan governor\u2019s race from Toss-up to **Lean Democratic**, with Jocelyn Benson described as the favorite to succeed Gretchen Whitmer, signaling a modest Democratic edge in statewide contests this cycle.[6][14] In the concurrent 2026 Senate race, available primary polling shows fluctuating leads between Abdul El-Sayed and Haley Stevens, but no consistent general-election head-to-head numbers versus a named Republican within the last 45 days; combined with forecasters labeling Michigan a \"core swing state\" yet competitive, this supports a slight Democratic lean but not a safe advantage.[12][3][10][13] With no fresh general-election polling, the best proxy margin is the small Democratic edge implied by recent ratings changes (Toss-up to Lean D) and descriptions of Benson as a slight favorite, which I represent as roughly a 2-point Democratic advantage in the current environment, while emphasizing that this is based on forecaster ratings and not direct head-to-head polls.[6][14]",
